{"content":[{"c":["ASYLUM*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Place of refuge where a fugitive from justice is immune to arrest or retribution; also, the protection afforded by such a place. An equivalent term is “sanctuary” (originally meaning “holy place”), from the ancient custom of seeking asylum at an altar or in a temple. Thus Adonijah (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.1.50-53","r":"1Kgs.1.50-53","rawR":"1Kgs.1.50-53","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.1.50-53","value":"1Kgs.1.50-53"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 1:50-53"},") and Joab (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.2.28-31","r":"1Kgs.2.28-31","rawR":"1Kgs.2.28-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.2.28-31","value":"1Kgs.2.28-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 2:28-31"},") both sought sanctuary from King Solomon at the altar of the tabernacle. In the law of Moses asylum was provided through the establishment of cities of refuge. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Cities of Refuge"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Asylum","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 1:50-53","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.1.50-53","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.1.50-53","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.1.50-53"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 2:28-31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.2.28-31","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.2.28-31","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.2.28-31"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d362b8abecca0f281c629ec6b90b5d3e9170e30a36c2c05f9b14bec54ec77a4e","sourceItemName":"Asylum","sourceItemOrder":591,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Asylum","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Asylum*","title":"Asylum*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}